par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, altcoins, led by memecoins and AI-themed cryptocurrencies, have outperformed BTC over the last week, initiating a debate on whether the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/data-points-to-approaching-altcoin-season-even-as-bitcoin-dominance-holds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 altcoin season}}}\uc2  (altseason) is here.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-03/c8b3156f-5da9-421e-ac0f-b73c97e5ad68.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/PzSG3UXb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Total crypto market capitalization hits $2.5 trillion\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s brief escapade above $69,000 on March 5 saw the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-recaptures-2-trillion-market-cap-bitcoin-climbs-above-57000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 global crypto market value cross the $2.5 trillion mark}}}\uc2 , reflecting the current \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum. At the time of publishing, this figure stands at $2.52 trillion, according to data from CoinMarketCap.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-03/00d2145c-0eb4-4179-91df-06b3053115fa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Total crypto market capitalization. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/9QCFeEMK/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/what-is-an-altcoin-a-beginners-guide-to-cryptocurrencies-beyond-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Altcoins}}}\uc2  displayed similar strength, with their total market capitalization (see chart below) rising above $1.1 trillion on the same day. This metric measures the total market value of all crypto assets except Bitcoin.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-03/5457b72f-018c-4023-8867-e8c209f87bf7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Total crypto market cap minus Bitcoin. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/I1J1eLkm/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Over the last three months, this value has rallied approximately 64% from $697 billion to $1.14 trillion on March 7. This is a slightly better performance than the 56% posted by Bitcoin over the same period.\par \par \uc2 This ascent attests to growing investor interest in altcoins and the amazing performance recently displayed by this class of crypto assets.\par \par \uc2 Large-cap altcoins outperform Bitcoin\par \par \uc2 The tremendous rally displayed by memecoins and AI over the last week could be a sign that the market is at the start of the altseason.\par \par \uc2 Data from CoinMarketCap shows memecoins posting double and triple-digit gains within the last seven days.\par \par \uc2 In particular, Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) and Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) posted 20% and 130% gains this week, respectively. Newer tokens such as Pepe ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/pepe-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 PEPE}}}\uc2  ), Bonk (BONK) and Dogwifhat (WIF) saw double to triple-digit gains during the same period.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-03/318613b2-104d-4f06-b7ba-03078e51b74c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Top memecoins\u8217\'20\'19 7-day performance. Source: CoinMarketCap\par \par \uc2 Other notable performances came from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ai-tokens-rally-amid-nvidia-breakout-earnings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tokens within the AI ecosystem}}}\uc2  led by Fetch.ai (FET), Synesis One (SNS), SingularityNET (AGIX) and Theta Network ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/theta-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 THETA}}}\uc2  ), which also produced double to triple-digit gains in 7 days.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has only risen 8.5% over the same period.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not altseason... yet\par \par \uc2 The performance of the altcoins seemingly coincides with an improvement in the altcoin season index, indicating that the altcoin season is close. According to this index by Blockchain Center:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf 75% of the top 50 coins performed better than Bitcoin over the last season (90 days), it is Altcoin Season.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-03/96c51569-24f9-4851-b34f-ffbe1f3c6da8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Altcoin season index. Source: Blockchain Center\par \par \uc2 This indicator essentially demonstrates that only 69% of the leading 50 altcoins have outperformed Bitcoin in the past 90 days. Although this index has increased over the last few days, it is still insufficient to declare an altcoin season.\par \par \uc2 However, according to a recent market {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://k33.com/research/articles/market-exuberance?product=pro&checkout=success"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  by K33 Research, this could change soon. The report noted that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-market-cap-new-high-surpassing-silver"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s rally toward its new all-time high}}}\uc2  saw its market cap double relative to the value of all cryptocurrencies except BTC and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) since the bottom of November 2022.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-accumulation-phase-ends-etfs-100k-btc-price-target"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin accumulation phase ends as ETFs fuel new $100K BTC price target}}}\par \par \uc2 The K33 Research analysts said the setup mirrors the 2020 altcoin bull run just before they caught up with Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s uptrend.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJudging by history, altcoins will start outperforming about the time we are now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-03/a0021890-dcae-4b9f-ac91-4e7e18a1a193.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC vs. altcoins market cap. Source: K33 Research\par \par \uc2 Independent analyst CrediBULL dives into the connection between Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s performance at the start of the altseason. In a March 4 post in X, CrediBULL {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CredibleCrypto/status/1764720563564495294?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlines}}}\uc2  two possible scenarios:\par \par \uc2 A mega breakout when Bitcoin breaks its prior ATH and quickly doubles in a matter of weeks, and \u8220\'20\'1Calts don't get much love until BTC pauses after this breakout leg,\u8221\'20\'1D and a consolidation scenario where Bitcoin revisits its prior ATH but faces rejection or consolidates at the highs for a few weeks. In the latter case, altcoins \u8220\'20\'1Cstart rallying almost immediately after BTC tags prior to ATH. \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 CrediBull sais:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe common theme here and the key takeaway is that after BTC hits prior ATH, alts begin rallying at the first major pause/consolidation of BTC, whether that at prior ATH or far above it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, founder and CEO of MN Trading Consultancy Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe believes that the altcoin season is yet to kick in, pointing out that they still have \u8220\'20\'1C40-60% market capitalization\u8221\'20\'1D before it reaches the 2021 highs above $1.1 trillion.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-03/ba25282e-f87c-47ac-8688-1dde6fc3a81c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Altcoin market cap excluding BTC and ETH. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1765728607010234712?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe on X}}}\par \par \uc2 On his part, Cardano founder \uc2 Charles Hoskinson\uc2  believes that the altcoin season will start once DOGE overtakes \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  in market capitalization. In a March 5 post on X social media platform, Hoskinson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/IOHK_Charles/status/1764821346385854533?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat moment DOGE flips Cardano. It\u8217\'20\'19s officially alt-season kids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDMvNzIzNTg4YjUtYmE3Mi00MTc1LTliYWUtMWU2NjQzNjQyNjJjLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240311ek370000t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Altcoins\par \b \uc2 Altseason is coming \u8212\'20\'14 or at least data suggests that its close\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Nancy Lubale \par \uc2 874 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 March 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Is it altseason? Not yet, but data hints that it is coming.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) price witnessed a sharp correction shortly after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-all