\par\par \b \uc2 Pandoshi (PAMBO) Set To Perform Better Than Cardano ( \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 ) in 2024\b0\par\par\uc2 Crypto Daily \par \uc2 598 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 January 2024\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2024, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pandoshi (PAMBO)}}}\par \par \uc2 As the cryptocurrency market continues to evolve, emerging players like Pandoshi (PAMBO) are setting the stage for a dynamic shift in the world of digital assets. Heading into 2024, Pandoshi, with its innovative and comprehensive DeFi ecosystem, is being eyed as a potential competitor to established giants such as Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). Built on a Layer-2 network utilizing Proof of Stake protocol, Pandoshi's strategic approach towards decentralization, environmental sustainability, and community-driven governance has not only distinguished it from its peers but also positioned it as a promising candidate for significant performance and growth in the coming year.\par \par \uc2 With its recent achievements, including a successful presale and the launch of the Pandoshi Wallet, the project is rapidly gaining traction among investors and blockchain enthusiasts, hinting at a potentially remarkable performance that could rival, if not surpass, Cardano's success.\par \par \uc2 Pandoshi (PAMBO)\par \par \uc2 Pandoshi is quickly making its mark in the cryptocurrency world, having successfully raised over $2 million in just a couple of weeks. This impressive feat demonstrates the market's growing trust in its potential. Standing as a paradigm of blockchain's founding values, Pandoshi emphasizes decentralization, privacy, and user empowerment in a community-driven framework.\par \par \uc2 The ecosystem of Pandoshi is diverse, featuring a Layer-2 network based on the Proof of Stake model, a user-centric decentralized exchange, a non-custodial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tinyurl.com/pandoshiwallet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pandoshi Wallet}}}\uc2 , engaging Metaverse gaming experiences, and Pandoshi University for educational resources. The ecosystem is further enhanced by its crypto-compatible prepaid cards, designed to facilitate global \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  management without requiring KYC procedures.\par \par \uc2 Currently, Pandoshi is navigating through its carefully planned presale, which is organized into five phases. The token is currently priced at $0.008 in the fourth phase, and it's anticipated that the price will rise to $0.01 in the next and final phase, marking a crucial step for the project.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tinyurl.com/pandoshicrpdaily25"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here}}}\par \par \uc2 Central to the Pandoshi ecosystem is the PAMBO token. It serves as the main currency within the PandaChain, the Metaverse Game, and for transactions at Pandoshi University, benefiting from the buy-and-burn strategy used by PandoshiSwap and Cardoshi. With its deflationary nature, PAMBO is available for purchase directly or through participation in Pandoshi's activities.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, Pandoshi has introduced BAMBOO, a governance token allowing community members to steer the project's direction. In contrast to PAMBO, BAMBOO is inflationary with no predetermined supply limit and is obtained through the staking of PAMBO tokens.\par \par \uc2 Pandoshi has recently taken a significant step forward by launching the beta version of its Pandoshi Wallet on the \uc2 Google\uc2  Play Store, with an iOS release soon to follow. This development, occurring during the presale phase, has effectively dispelled skepticism among investors, demonstrating the project's capability to deliver on its promises ahead of schedule.\par \par \uc2 The wallet's introduction, especially during this crucial phase, is a testament to the team's commitment and ability to achieve milestones, reinforcing trust in the project's future. This launch, supporting both \uc2 EVM\uc2  and non-EVM chains, marks a pivotal moment in Pandoshi's journey, showcasing its potential and readiness to innovate and lead in the cryptocurrency space.\par \par \uc2 Click Here To Buy PAMBO Tokens\par \par \uc2 Visit the links below for more information about Pandoshi (PAMBO):\par \par \uc2 Website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pandoshi.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://pandoshi.com/}}}\par \par \uc2 Whitepaper: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.pandoshi.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://docs.pandoshi.com/}}}\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This is a sponsored press release and is for informational purposes only. It does not reflect the views of Crypto Daily, nor is it intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, or financial advice.\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020240123ek1m00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Elliott Stein\par \b \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has 70% chance of full dismissal in SEC lawsuit \u8212\'20\'14 Litigation analyst\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Ciaran Lyons \par \uc2 598 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 January 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Stein explains it was a turning point when \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  provided a more precise definition of an \u8220\'20\'1Cinvestment contract\u8221\'20\'1D than the SEC.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg senior litigation analyst Elliott Stein has indicated he sees minimal likelihood of failure for cryptocurrency exchange \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  in its ongoing lawsuit against the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC). Stein forecasts a 70% chance of the exchange securing a full dismissal in the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/NYCStein/status/1748334299957367287?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  on Jan. 19 on X (formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ), Stein explained that before he entered the courtroom, he was confident that \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  could object successfully to certain SEC claims but not those allegations relating to its staking rewards program and overall operational structure.\par \par \uc2 However, his confidence shifted after the five-hour hearing:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI went into SEC v. \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  hearing thinking COIN would, on this motion, win dismissal of SEC's primary claims (concerning trading) but maybe not staking and broker claims. I left thinking COIN would win full dismissal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The SEC alleges that by staking customer assets, earning rewards on their behalf and returning them, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  is engaging in offering and selling investment contracts, thereby falling under SEC \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, the regulator alleges that \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  was operating as an unregistered broker. Meanwhile, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has strongly refuted this, stating there is no easy way for a crypto exchange to register for a license.\par \par \uc2 However, Stein explains it was a turning point when \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  provided a more precise definition of an \u8220\'20\'1Cinvestment contract\u8221\'20\'1D than the SEC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy view the one offered by \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  as more compelling, requiring investment in a business vs. just an ecosystem, along with an enforceable obligation,\u8221\'20\'1D he stated.\par \par \uc2 Greetings from federal court in Lower Manhattan! Today's episode: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/coinbase?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @coinbase}}}\uc2  motion to toss the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SECGov?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SECGov}}}\uc2  suit. Should be a great (4hr long!) argument, with top lawyering, a fascinating/unsettled legal q, & Judge Failla - sharp as a knife & a sense of humor drier than the Sahara. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qwR4q4ZAkh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qwR4q4ZAkh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elliott Z. Stein (@NYCStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NYCStein/status/1747627532508176635?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 However, he referenced the recent SEC vs. \uc2 Ripple\uc2  case, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/the-sec-vs-ripple-lawsuit-everything-you-need-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ripple achieved a partial victory}}}\uc2  in July 2023. The judge ruled that XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) is not considered a security when it comes to retail sales on cryptocurrency exchanges.\par \par \uc2 Stein suggests the decision around securities, in this case, will have a domino effect on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit, too.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the \uc2 Ripple\uc2  ruling in July suggested, sales of digital assets on public exchanges don\u8217\'20\'19t fit neatly into the Howey test for what constitutes an investment contract,\u8221\'20\'1D he argued.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-biz-coinbase-sec-determine-crypto-tokens-fate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto Biz: Coinbase vs. SEC case will determine crypto tokens fate}}}\par \par \uc2 On Jan. 17, Cointelegraph reported that U.S. District Judge \uc2 Katherine Polk Failla\uc2  heard arguments {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-hearing-sec-arguments-highlight-court-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the SEC and Coinbase}}}\uc2  on the crypto exchange\u8217\'20\'19s motion for dismissal over a period of five hours.\par \par \uc2 In a notable point for the crypto community, Failla asked the SEC attorneys to explain why a digital token issuance would meet the Howey test, arguing the case was \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo broad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-coinbase-crypto-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC filed a lawsuit against Coinbase}}}\uc2  on June 6, 2023, alleging the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-dispute-sec-crypto-authority-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto exchange violated federal securities laws}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The agency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908.1.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  that 13 tokens listed on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  were securities, including \uc2 Solana\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), Filecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/filecoin-fil-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FIL}}}\uc2  ), The Sandbox ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/the-sandbox-sand-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SAND}}}\uc2  ), Axie Infinity ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/axie-infinity-axs-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AXS}}}\uc2  ), Chiliz (CHZ), Flow ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/flow-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FLOW}}}\uc2  ), Internet Computer ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/internet-computer-icp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ICP}}}\uc2  ), Near ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/near-protocol-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NEAR}}}\uc2  ), Voyager (VGX), Dash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/dash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DASH}}}\uc2  ) and Nexo ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/nexo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NEXO}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/coinbase-fights-sec-in-court-sbfs-parents-seek-lawsuit-dismissal-and-bitcoin-etfs-hodlers-digest-jan-14-20/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase fights SEC in court, SBF\u8217\'20\'19s parents seek lawsuit dismissal, and Bitcoin ETFs: Hodler\u8217\'20\'19s Digest, Jan. 14-20}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDEvOWE2ZTQ2ZDQtMDA2Yi00YmZkLWI5YTgtNjQ1NzZkYzFkNzQ5LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240121ek1l0002u\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Elliott Stein\par \b \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has 70% chance of full dismissal in SEC lawsuit: Litigation analyst\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Ciaran Lyons \par \uc2 619 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 January 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Litigation analyst, Elliott Stein, clarified that \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  provided a more thorough explanation of what constitutes an investment contract, while predicting a 70% likelihood of a full dismissal in the case against the SEC.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg senior litigation analyst, Elliott Stein, has indicated he sees minimal likelihood of failure for cryptocurrency exchange \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  in its ongoing lawsuit against \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC). Stein forecasts a 70% chance of the exchange securing a full dismissal in the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 In a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/NYCStein/status/1748334299957367287?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  on Jan. 19 on X (formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ), Stein explained that before he went into the courtroom he was confident that \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  would be able to object successfully to certain SEC claims, but not those allegations relating to its staking rewards program and overall operational structure.\par \par \uc2 However, his confidence shifted after the five-hour hearing:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI went into SEC v. \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  hearing thinking COIN would, on this motion, win dismissal of SEC's primary claims (concerning trading) but maybe not staking and broker claims. I left thinking COIN would win full dismissal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The SEC alleges that by staking customers' assets, earning rewards on their behalf, and then returning them, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  is engaging in the offer and sale of investment contracts, thereby falling under SEC \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, the regulator alleges that \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  was operating as an unregistered broker. Meanwhile, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has strongly refuted this, stating there is no easy way for a crypto exchange to register for a license.\par \par \uc2 However, Stein explains that it was a turning point when \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  provided a more precise definition of an "investment contract" compared to the SEC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy view the one offered by \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  as more compelling, requiring investment in a business vs. just an ecosystem, along with an enforceable obligation,\u8221\'20\'1D he stated.\par \par \uc2 Greetings from federal court in Lower Manhattan! Today's episode: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/coinbase?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @coinbase}}}\uc2  motion to toss the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SECGov?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SECGov}}}\uc2  suit. Should be a great (4hr long!) argument, with top lawyering, a fascinating/unsettled legal q, & Judge Failla - sharp as a knife & a sense of humor drier than the Sahara. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qwR4q4ZAkh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qwR4q4ZAkh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elliott Z. Stein (@NYCStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NYCStein/status/1747627532508176635?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 However, he referenced the recent Ripple v SEC case where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/the-sec-vs-ripple-lawsuit-everything-you-need-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ripple achieved a partial victory}}}\uc2  in July 2023. The judge ruled that XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) is not considered a security when it comes to retail sales on cryptocurrency exchanges.\par \par \uc2 Stein suggests the decision around securities in this case, will have a domino effect into \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 's lawsuit too.\par \par \uc2 "As the \uc2 Ripple\uc2  ruling in July suggested, sales of digital assets on public exchanges don't fit neatly into the Howey test for what constitutes an investment contract," he argued.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-biz-coinbase-sec-determine-crypto-tokens-fate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto Biz: Coinbase vs. SEC case will determine crypto tokens fate}}}\par \par \uc2 On Jan. 17, Cointelegraph reported that United States District Judge \uc2 Katherine Polk Failla\uc2  heard arguments {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-hearing-sec-arguments-highlight-court-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the SEC and Coinbase}}}\uc2  on the crypto exchange\u8217\'20\'19s motion for dismissal over a period of five hours.\par \par \uc2 In a notable point for the crypto community, Failla asked the SEC attorneys to explain why a digital token issuance would meet the Howey test, arguing the case was \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo broad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-coinbase-crypto-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC filed a lawsuit against Coinbase}}}\uc2  on June 6, 2023, alleging that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-dispute-sec-crypto-authority-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto exchange violated federal securities laws.}}}\par \par \uc2 The agency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908.1.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  that 13 tokens listed on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  were securities, including coins like Solana (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ), Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), Polygon (MATIC), Filecoin (FIL), The Sandbox (SAND), Axie Infinity (AXS), Chiliz (CHZ), Flow (FLOW), Internet Computer (ICP), NEAR (NEAR), Voyager (VGX), Dash (DASH) and Nexo (NEXO).\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/coinbase-fights-sec-in-court-sbfs-parents-seek-lawsuit-dismissal-and-bitcoin-etfs-hodlers-digest-jan-14-20/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase fights SEC in court, SBF\u8217\'20\'19s parents seek lawsuit dismissal, and Bitcoin ETFs: Hodler\u8217\'20\'19s Digest, Jan. 14-20}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDEvOWE2ZTQ2ZDQtMDA2Yi00YmZkLWI5YTgtNjQ1NzZkYzFkNzQ5LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240121ek1l00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
