em Continues Expansion\par \par \uc2 The Optimism (OP) token and ecosystem have been one of the best performers in the past months. At the beginning of January, the Optimism (OP) token was trading at $4.03 on January 2. As the Bitcoin Spot ETF was approved on January 10, the Optimism (OP) price also surged along with the market.\par \par \uc2 By January 11, the Optimism (OP) token rose by nearly 5% to trade at $4.23 before correcting again. On January 14, the Optimism (OP) token was down by 18.1% to reach $3.50. Amid the OP correction, \uc2 Vitalik Buterin\uc2  spoke about Optimism RetroPGF round 3, which had distributed over $100 million on January 12. The first on-chain RWA, 3DNS, was released on the Optimism network on January 12 as well.\par \par \uc2 Due to these developments, experts are \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Optimism (OP) token going forward. They predict the Optimism (OP) token will rise above $5 in 2024.\par \par \uc2 For the latest updates and more information, be sure to visit the officialRebel Satoshi Presale Website or contact Rebel Red via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.me/RBLZRED"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here}}}\uc2  Telegram\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This is a sponsored press release and is for informational purposes only. It does not reflect the views of Crypto Daily, nor is it intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, or financial advice.\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020240118ek1i000ru\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Coinbase\par \b \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  argues stocks, Terraform Labs and Howey in 5-hour SEC face-off\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Ana Paula Pereira \par \uc2 1,109 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 January 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge \uc2 Katherine Polk Failla\uc2  has heard arguments from the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  over a motion to dismiss a lawsuit filed by the regulator in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 United States District Judge \uc2 Katherine Polk Failla\uc2  has heard arguments from the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  on the crypto exchange\u8217\'20\'19s motion for dismissal of a lawsuit filed by the regulator in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 The hearing was held for nearly five hours and provided an extensive overview of the key arguments in courts regarding the crypto space, assets and the SEC's role in regulating the industry.\par \par \uc2 During the hearing, Judge Failla critically examined the regulator\u8217\'20\'19s case against the crypto exchange, asking the SEC attorneys to explain why a digital token issuance would meet the Howey test, arguing the case was \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo broad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s view, buyers of tokens are also investing in the network or ecosystem behind it, indicating there is a value proposition behind a token purchase. \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorneys, however, challenged the argument, claiming that Bitcoin \u8212\'20\'14 described as a commodity by an SEC attorney during the hearing \u8212\'20\'14 is also backed by a community and has a network.\par \par \uc2 Judge Failla delved into the definition of staking and secondary market transactions, as well as recent court rulings involving crypto firms, such as the \uc2 Ripple\uc2  and Terraform Labs case. Cointelegraph has summarized the hearing\u8217\'20\'19s hottest topics below.\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  is trying to create a different Howey test, says SEC\par \par \uc2 Attorneys representing the SEC argued that the exchange is trying to create a different version of the Howey test while allowing trade of crypto tokens that offer holders access to ecosystems that the regulator described as a "common enterprise."\par \par \uc2 The SEC argued that the exchange independently conducted the Howey test, leading to differing interpretations regarding the status of certain tokens. This discrepancy in conclusions over the tokens regarding the test, according to the SEC, provides sufficient grounds to reject the motion and allow the case to proceed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe think they\u8217\'20\'19re making up a new test, and we believe that our position is the one that\u8217\'20\'19s most faithful and consistent, but in fact, compelled by the Howey test. It\u8217\'20\'19s not just a plausible reading, as they claim it is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 SEC v {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/coinbase?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @coinbase}}}\uc2  Update IV\par \par \uc2 In an unusual move, the Judge dispensed with any prepared arguments from either side and instead went straight to questioning the lawyers.\par \par \uc2 The first 2 hours was spent exclusively questioning of the SEC lawyers.\par \par \uc2 The SEC lawyers were better prepared\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MetaLawMan (@MetaLawMan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MetaLawMan/status/1747670652708933731?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Terraform Labs case enters the stage\par \par \uc2 During the hearing, the SEC discussed a recent ruling on Terraform Labs that concluded it sold digital assets as securities without registration. The decision, according to the SEC, provided further grounds for its case against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The topic was heavily discussed over the hearing. As per SEC attorneys, the cases of \uc2 Ripple\uc2  and Terraform Labs may differ from \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 's one, but the Howey test applies exactly in the same way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur perspective is they\u8217\'20\'19re identical in terms of the Howey test that applies," said the SEC. "We think \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  is trying to create a different Howey test for when the people at this table might sell the tokens to each other on its platform and when Terraform might sell its tokens on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s platform.\par \par \uc2 And we think that\u8217\'20\'19s just wrong, your honor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal team argued that Terraform Labs\u8217\'20\'19 case did not involve secondary market transactions, such as the ones conducted on the \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  platform. Another key difference appointed in court is that, in Terraform Labs' dispute, investors and the company were in a private relationship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut the Terraform case, first of all, as I know the court knows, did not involve secondary market transactions," they argued.\par \par \uc2 There were no secondary market transactions in that case. [...] Those were all situations where there was a relationship between the investor and the promoter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In addition, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  counsel explored the legal requirements for establishing an investment contract under U.S. law, which requires a type of financial arrangement where an individual invests money in a venture managed by another party with the expectation of earning a profit.\par \par \uc2 "An investment contract, at a minimum, requires the contracting parties to agree or scheme together that the contractee will invest in the contractor\u8217\'20\'19s profit-seeking endeavor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 , users trading tokens on its platform may or may not seek profit on the investment, as tokens can also be acquired for their utility. Judge Failla added that investors can purchase tokens because they are \u8220\'20\'1Ccool\u8221\'20\'1D or because a friend owns them.\par \par \uc2 Ripple\uc2 , stocks and more talks over secondary market transactions\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  argued that token holders don't receive dividends or have legal rights over a project just because they own tokens, which is different from stocks.\par \par \uc2 "A stock reflects an interest in the permanent capital of a corporation. And when it trades, that interest in the permanent capital of the corporation, which is a participation in its capital structure, transferred in entirety from one holder to another holder."\par \par \uc2 The discussion over stocks and crypto tokens stemmed from \uc2 Ripple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ruling from July 2023, when Judge Analisa Torres granted a summary judgment in favor of \uc2 Ripple Labs\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ripple-wins-case-against-sec-as-judge-rules-xrp-is-not-a-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 determining that the XRP token is not a security when sold via programmatic sales on exchanges}}}\uc2 . However, Judge Torres also found that XRP was a security when sold to institutional investors, aligning with the criteria of the Howey Test.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-senator-warren-allegations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase refutes Senator Warren\u8217\'20\'19s government insider allegations}}}\par \par \uc2 "The critical takeaway there is that Judge Torres recognized that secondary market token purchases of XRP were not investing in \uc2 Ripple\uc2 . And in that sense, it rejected what I think is a core portion of the Commission's argument before the court today, which is its investment in an ecosystem, at least with respect to transactions between strangers, where no relationship exists, where no obligations travel."\par \par \uc2 In \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 's view, blind trades between individuals on its platform does not constitute an investment agreement.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-coinbase-crypto-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC sued Coinbase}}}\uc2  on June 6, 2023, alleging that the cryptocurrency exchange violated federal securities laws. The agency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908.1.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  that 13 tokens listed on the exchange were securities, including coins like Solana (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ), Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), Polygon (MATIC), Filecoin (FIL), The Sandbox (SAND), Axie Infinity (AXS), Chiliz (CHZ), Flow (FLOW), Internet Computer (ICP), NEAR (NEAR), \uc2 Voyager\uc2  (VGX), Dash (DASH) and Nexo (NEXO).\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/crypto-regulation-sec-chair-gary-gensler-final-say/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto \b  \highlight22regulation\b0 \highlight22  \u8212\'20\'14 Does SEC Chair Gary Gensler have the final say?}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS9zdG9yYWdlL3VwbG9hZHMvdmlldy9jNzU2Y2NlNmYwZTgzMjU1OWZmNzcwZDQ2MTQ1YWY2NC5qcGc=.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240118ek1h00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Coinbase\par \b \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  to dispute SEC crypto authority in federal court\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Ana Paula Pereira \par \uc2 529 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 January 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and the \uc2 U.S. SEC\uc2  will appear in court for a hearing on Jan. 17. According to \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 , the lawsuit should be dismissed.\par \par \uc2 Crypto exchange \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) will appear in court for a hearing that will determine the next steps in the case.\par \par \uc2 On Jan. 17 at 10 am ET (3 pm UTC), a court in New York is expected to hear oral arguments on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s motion to dismiss the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit against the exchange. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-coinbase-crypto-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC sued Coinbase}}}\uc2  on June 6, 2023, alleging that the cryptocurrency exchange violated federal securities laws.\par \par \uc2 The agency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908.1.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  that 13 tokens listed on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  were securities, including coins like Solana (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ), Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), Polygon (MATIC), Filecoin (FIL), The Sandbox (SAND), Axie Infinity (AXS), Chiliz (CHZ), Flow (FLOW), Internet Computer (ICP), NEAR (NEAR), Voyager (VGX), Dash (DASH) and Nexo (NEXO).\par \par \uc2 According to Jeremy Hogan, partner at Hogan and Hogan, motions to dismiss \u8220\'20\'1Care rarely granted,\u8221\'20\'1D however, district judge Katherine Polk Faill has a background in dismissing crypto cases. She granted a motion to dismiss a case against Uniswap for allegedly selling \u8220\'20\'1Cscam tokens\u8221\'20\'1D back in 2013.\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  is seeking an order to drop the case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-to-file-order-seeking-dismissal-of-sec-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questioning the SEC's authority over crypto exchanges}}}\uc2  and noting that the regulator never suggested a requirement to register as a securities exchange when it approved \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s registration statement in April 2021. According to Hogan, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has some chances to win despite U.S. courts rarely dismissing lawsuits.\par \par \uc2 The SEC v. Coinbase BIG motion to dismiss hearing is Wednesday morning. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MetaLawMan?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MetaLawMan}}}\uc2  will be there live!\par \par \uc2 Motions to Dismiss are rarely granted so I wasn't expecting much. HOWEVER, I just looked at a prior Order on a motion to dismiss from the same Judge on a crypto case and...\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeremy Hogan (@attorneyjeremy1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/attorneyjeremy1/status/1746943405291106490?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBased on this Judge's prior dismissal of the Uniswap case, her clear understanding of the technology, her finding that Eth is a commodity, and acknowledgement that Congress should be involved in this process\u8230\'20\'26 I'll be very interested to see how this plays out,\u8221\'20\'1D Hogan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/attorneyjeremy1/status/1746943412157259815?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on X on Jan. 15.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI won\u8217\'20\'19t predict how Judge Failla will rule on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s motion to dismiss until after the hearing tomorrow. But, one thing I can confidently predict, the Judge will pose some tough questions to the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers,\u8221\'20\'1D crypto legal expert MetaLawMan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/MetaLawMan/status/1747295108683227291?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on X.\par \par \uc2 The case is part of the SEC's crackdown on crypto firms that has been taking place since \uc2 FTX\uc2  collapsed in November 2022. The case could seal the fate of several crypto tokens in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 , the SEC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-consider-terraform-labs-ruling-binance-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is taking the same approach as in the Binance case}}}\uc2 , asking the court to consider a recent ruling on Terraform Labs that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-us-court-rules-favor-sec-do-kwon-terraform-labs-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 determined the company sold securities without registration}}}\uc2 . The decision, according to the SEC, provided further grounds for its cases against the crypto exchanges.\par \par \uc2 Additional reporting by Helen Partz.\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/crypto-regulation-sec-chair-gary-gensler-final-say/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto \b  \highlight22regulation\b0 \highlight22  \u8212\'20\'14 Does SEC Chair Gary Gensler have the final say?}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDEvMjVmNzY1OWItZWYxMC00OGE4LTg3NGQtN2UwMmFlM2Q1NzNhLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020240117ek1h0008f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
